# .graphifyignore — controls what the graphify knowledge graph indexes.
# Same syntax as .gitignore (merged with it; patterns here win on conflict).
#
# NOTE ON DOCS: The committed graph is an OFFLINE, code-only AST graph (built
# without an LLM backend, so it has zero API cost and rebuilds deterministically
# via the post-commit hook / `graphify update .`). Markdown, HTML, PDFs, and
# images require an LLM and are excluded below. To enrich the graph with docs,
# remove the "Docs & data" and "Markup/data treated as docs" blocks and run
# `/graphify .` inside an IDE session (or `graphify extract .` with an API key).

# ── Vendored / generated ─────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
.git/
graphify-out/
**/.next/
**/out/
**/dist/
**/build/
**/.remotion/
**/Pods/
recovery-ios/App/
capacitor/ios/

# ── Vendored / synced third-party skill bundles (not product code) ───
# Source-of-truth + symlinked skill bundles synced from upstreams
# (huggingface/skills, anthropics/skills, mattpocock/skills, ...). Tracked in
# skills-lock.json; they otherwise dominate the graph (~17k nodes) and bury the
# actual RHYTHMIX / Studio / app code.
.agents/skills/
.claude/skills/
.superpowers/

# ── Vendored minified libraries (noise) ──────────────────────────────
**/*.min.js
**/gsap*.js
**/three*.js

# ── Docs & data (need an LLM backend — not available offline) ─────────
*.md
*.mdx
*.rst
*.txt
*.pdf
*.csv
*.xsd

# ── Markup/data treated as docs by graphify (need an LLM) ─────────────
*.html
*.htm
*.yaml
*.yml
*.qmd

# ── Binary / media assets ─────────────────────────────────────────────
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.gif
*.webp
*.svg
*.ico
*.icns
*.mp3
*.mp4
*.mov
*.wav
*.ttf
*.otf
*.woff
*.woff2
*.zip
*.gz
